{"Title":"An Act establishing comprehensive school counseling programs","BillNumber":"H465","DocketNumber":"HD3568","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CAD1","Name":"Carol A. Doherty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CAD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T13:28:44.187"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CAD1","Name":"Carol A. Doherty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CAD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T13:28:44.1866667"},{"Id":"RMH2","Name":"Ryan M. Hamilton","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RMH2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T13:28:44.3566667"},{"Id":"ACM1","Name":"Adrian C. Madaro","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/ACM1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-06T16:19:39.9066667"},{"Id":"JCD1","Name":"James C. Arena-DeRosa","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JCD1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-09T12:12:18.1533333"},{"Id":"JKH1","Name":"James K. Hawkins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JKH1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-09T12:13:08.0166667"},{"Id":"RME1","Name":"Rodney M. Elliott","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RME1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-19T13:22:24.0266667"},{"Id":"SPK1","Name":"Sally P. Kerans","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SPK1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-27T23:22:17.9733333"},{"Id":"SBA1","Name":"Shirley B. Arriaga","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SBA1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-27T23:20:58.8566667"},{"Id":"S_G1","Name":"Sean Garballey","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/S_G1","ResponseDate":"2023-03-09T10:18:29.3033333"},{"Id":"WFT0","Name":"Walter F. Timilty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WFT0","ResponseDate":"2023-03-14T11:04:56.14"},{"Id":"APR1","Name":"Adrianne Pusateri Ramos","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/APR1","ResponseDate":"2023-04-05T10:28:49.1033333"},{"Id":"S_M1","Name":"Samantha Montaño","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/S_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-04-22T15:08:30.5133333"},{"Id":"DAS1","Name":"Danillo A. Sena","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DAS1","ResponseDate":"2023-07-21T12:43:24.47"},{"Id":"AXV1","Name":"Andres X. Vargas","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AXV1","ResponseDate":"2023-09-05T15:42:10.3166667"},{"Id":"L_S1","Name":"Lindsay N. Sabadosa","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_S1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-03T10:52:27.4366667"},{"Id":"MRS1","Name":"Margaret R. Scarsdale","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MRS1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-17T16:56:41.8666667"},{"Id":"PAD1","Name":"Patricia A. Duffy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PAD1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-17T16:56:35"},{"Id":"DMD1","Name":"Daniel M. Donahue","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DMD1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-17T16:27:57.6133333"},{"Id":"PJK1","Name":"Patrick Joseph Kearney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJK1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-31T13:50:34.1766667"},{"Id":"NMB1","Name":"Natalie M. Blais","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/NMB1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-31T13:50:26.4733333"},{"Id":"FEP1","Name":"Francisco E. Paulino","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/FEP1","ResponseDate":"2024-02-13T12:18:11.75"},{"Id":"SCO1","Name":"Steven Owens","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SCO1","ResponseDate":"2024-02-13T12:18:04.6933333"},{"Id":"N_H1","Name":"Natalie M. Higgins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_H1","ResponseDate":"2024-02-22T13:13:29.16"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"RMH2","Name":"Ryan M. Hamilton","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RMH2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T13:28:44.187"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H465/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representatives Doherty of Taunton and Hamilton of Methuen, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 465) of Carol A. Doherty, Ryan M. Hamilton and others relative to establishing comprehensive school counseling programs.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 71 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition is hereby amended by inserting the following:-\r\n\t“Each public school district shall develop and implement a comprehensive school counseling program that adheres to the Massachusetts Model for Comprehensive School Counseling Programs and ensures all pre-K to grade twelve (12) students will receive school counseling services from licensed school counselors. In accordance with the Model, each school counselor is to spend at least eighty percent (80%) of that school counselor’s time providing direct or indirect services to students. To maintain equity in student access to a school counselor, each district shall provide one (1) school counselor for a maximum of two hundred fifty (250) students, the nationally recommended average.”\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}